WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.030
In Darwin, northern Australia, January
brings a mean of 432 millimetres of rain.

2
00:00:07.080 --> 00:00:09.610
July brings 1 millimetre.

3
00:00:09.660 --> 00:00:14.030
Yet every month, the mean
maximum tops 30 degrees Celsius.

4
00:00:14.080 --> 00:00:17.800
The grass flushes green,
turns gold, and the dry,

5
00:00:17.850 --> 00:00:19.970
fire-prone months set in.

6
00:00:20.020 --> 00:00:25.410
On the Serengeti, in Tanzania, about 2
million wildebeest live with the same boom

7
00:00:25.460 --> 00:00:26.510
and bust.

8
00:00:26.560 --> 00:00:29.310
So how does life cope in the savanna?

9
00:00:29.360 --> 00:00:32.770
In this mission, you'll build a
soil moisture budget for an old,

10
00:00:32.820 --> 00:00:34.750
poor tropical soil.

11
00:00:34.800 --> 00:00:37.170
Then you'll follow
people into the savanna,

12
00:00:37.220 --> 00:00:41.790
from cattle grazing in Australia
to soy farms in Brazil's Cerrado.

13
00:00:41.840 --> 00:00:46.650
Your mission: explain how savanna life
copes with a year split between pouring

14
00:00:46.700 --> 00:00:48.590
rain and almost none.
